    "number": "Section 5.1 (A Lower bound)",
    "quote": "We show an $\\Omega(C)$ lower bound for the pseudo-regret of any algorithm. Consider the case of two arms with deterministic rewards $0$ and $1$, and consider an adversary that at each time step swaps the rewards of the arms with probability $1/2$. ... there is a lower bound of $\\Omega(C)$ that holds for all $C$ up to $T \\div 2$. Moreover this lower bound holds even for the case of known $C$."
